<title>USA: Duff &amp; Phelps may cut Energy Group, units.</title>
<headline>Duff &amp; Phelps may cut Energy Group, units.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Duff &amp; Phelps Credit Rating Co said Friday it may downgrade its implied senior unsecured debt rating of the Energy Group, its bond ratings of Eastern Electricity and its short-term ratings of Energy Group, Eastern and Peabody Finance Ltd.</p>
<p>The action, which follows a bid for London-based Energy Group by the U.S. group PacifiCorp, affects $900 million of existing long-term debt, Duff &amp; Phelps said. Eastern and Peabody are both owned by Energy Group.</p>
</text>
